"Gamarra, Luis Valenzuela","rank":216,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"23 108","corresponding":null,"first":"Kyle G.","key":"dexterkylegpau","last":"Dexter","name":"Dexter, Kyle G.","rank":217,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jbi.14816","issn":["03050270","13652699"],"issn_org":["03050270"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Biogeography","pages":"1163-1184","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biogeography","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85185958120"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-09f9f459-c9c6-4fe7-a648-8090cf140697"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Geography and ecology shape the phylogenetic composition of Amazonian tree communities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743628","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Time-based cryptographic primitives such as Time-Lock Puzzles (TLPs) and Verifiable Delay Functions (VDFs) have proven to be pivotal in several areas of cryptography. All existing candidate constructions, however, guarantee time-delays based on the average hardness of sequential computational problems. This means that any algorithmic or hardware improvement affects parameter choices and may turn deployed systems insecure. To address this issue, we investigate how to build time-based cryptographic primitives where delays depend on sources other than sequential computations: namely, transmission delays caused by sequential communication. We explore sequential communication delays that arise when sending a message through a constellation of satellites in Space. This setting has the advantage that distances between protocol participants are guaranteed as positions of satellites are observable from Earth, moreover delay lower bounds are unconditional and can be easily computed using the laws of Physics (the speed of light bounds transmission speed). We introduce proofs of sequential communication delay (SCD) in the Universal Composability framework, that can be used to convince a verifier that a message has accrued delay by traversing a path among a set of scattered satellites. With our SCD proofs we realize the first proposals of Publicly Verifiable TLPs and VDFs whose delay guarantees are rooted on physical limits, rather than ever-decreasing computational hardness. Finally, our notion of SCD paves the way to the first Delay Encryption construction not based on supersingular isogenies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Baum, Carsten","David, Bernardo Machado","Pagnin, Elena","Takahashi, Akira"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764114"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-13","place":"Amalfi, it","start":"2024-09-11","title":"14th International Conference on Security and Cryptography for Networks","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Baum, Carsten"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","J.P. Morgan Chase & Co."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cascade time based cryptography from space communications delay","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85204637805","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764114","identifier":[{"id":"85204637805","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-18fc7392-c071-4042-9fb0-c5c1ffb23e84"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6D07B68201A8523B522FC6DEAA06E44B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cybersecurity Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"j p morgan chase co","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"J.P. Morgan Chase & Co.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"baumpau","last":"Baum","locid":"ac00f0e9-1985-4767-922a-d55e5df81c29","name":"Baum, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-7905-0198","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo Machado","key":"davidpau","last":"David","name":"David, Bernardo Machado","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"pagninpau","last":"Pagnin","name":"Pagnin, Elena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Akira","key":"takahashipau","last":"Takahashi","name":"Takahashi, Akira","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-71070-4_12","eisbn":["9783031710704"],"isbn":["9783031710698"],"pages":"252-274","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 14th International Conference on Security and Cryptography for Networks (SCN 2024)","volume":"14973"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204637805"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-18fc7392-c071-4042-9fb0-c5c1ffb23e84"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"CaSCaDE: (Time-Based) Cryptography from Space Communications DElay","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764114","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We describe the geographical variation in tree species composition across Amazonian forests and show how environmental conditions are associated with species turnover. Our analyses are based on 2023 forest inventory plots (1 ha) that provide abundance data for a total of 5188 tree species. Within-plot species composition reflected both local environmental conditions (especially soil nutrients and hydrology) and geographical regions. A broader-scale view of species turnover was obtained by interpolating the relative tree species abundances over Amazonia into 47,441 0.1-degree grid cells. Two main dimensions of spatial change in tree species composition were identified. The first was a gradient between western Amazonia at the Andean forelands (with young geology and relatively nutrient-rich soils) and central-eastern Amazonia associated with the Guiana and Brazilian Shields (with more ancient geology and poor soils). The second gradient was between the wet forests of the northwest and the drier forests in southern Amazonia. Isolines linking cells of similar composition crossed major Amazonian rivers, suggesting that tree species distributions are not limited by rivers. Even though some areas of relatively sharp species turnover were identified, mostly the tree species composition changed gradually over large extents, which does not support delimiting clear discrete biogeographic regions within Amazonia.","author_count":225,"contributors":["Luize, Bruno Garcia","Tuomisto, Hanna","Ekelschot, Robin","Dexter, Kyle G.","Amaral, Iêda L.do","Coelho, Luiz de Souza","Matos, Francisca Dionízia de Almeida","Lima Filho, Diógenes de Andrade","Salomão, Rafael P.","Wittmann, Florian","Castilho, Carolina V.","Carim, Marcelo de Jesus Veiga","Guevara, Juan Ernesto","Phillips, Oliver L.","Magnusson, William E.","Sabatier, Daniel","Cardenas Revilla, Juan David","Molino, Jean François","Irume, Mariana Victória","Martins, Maria Pires","Guimarães, José Renan da Silva","Ramos, J